;;; theorem-library/measure-ch1-pullback.scm -- THE PULLBACK SIGMA-ALGEBRA AND THE PULLBACK MEASURE
;;; (M-A, wave MAP-1026, 2026-10-26).  Vocabulary: structure-library/measure-ch1-vocab.scm (PULLBACK-SIGMA,
;;; PULLBACK-MEASURE).  Source: Thayer, Construction of Measures, ch. 1, Prop. 1.14 and Prop. 1.22.
;;; Helper prefix: ma-.
;;;
;;; THE HEADLINES.
;;;   pullback-sigma-algebra        Prop. 1.14: cB a sigma-algebra on omega2, f in FUN(omega, omega2): the sets
;;;                                 f^-1(b), b in cB, form a sigma-algebra on omega, f is measurable for it, and it
;;;                                 is contained in every sigma-algebra on omega for which f is measurable.
;;;   pullback-measure-exists-unique
;;;                                 Prop. 1.22: nu a measure on (omega2, cB), f in FUN(omega, omega2) ONTO omega2:
;;;                                 PULLBACK-MEASURE (a |-> nu(f(a))) is a measure on the pullback with
;;;                                 f^-1(b) |-> nu(b), and it is the only measure on the pullback doing so.
;;;
;;; THE ROUTE.  For countable unions in 1.14 a member g(n) = f^-1(b) does not determine b, so the sequence of
;;; b's is chosen (CHOICE of the non-empty set of b's, abstracted to a function symbol); for 1.22 f onto makes
;;; f(f^-1(b)) = b (image-preimage-of-surjection), so the measure needs no choice, and the image of a countable
;;; union is the union of the images (image-of-countable-union).
;;;
;;; LOAD WINDOW.  lo: the vocabulary file (after structure-library/measure, injection); the latest citation is
;;; card-union-nn's file theorem-library/card-inequalities (load.scm 1386).  hi: none.  Library: measure.
;;;
;;; No top-level macro: the file may be compiled.

